  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Education for citizenship and human rights</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Instituto Bartolom&#xE9; de las Casas (IBC) was formed in 1974 with the support of Gustavo Guti&#xE9;rrez (the &#x2018;father of liberation theology&#x2019;) and has a long history of providing support and leadership training in popular participation to a wide range of Peruvian organisations.   It seeks to contribute to the construction of civil society and democracy in Peru, and to the empowerment of the poor, by offering a comprehensive programme of formation for Christian communities, social organisations, university students and young professionals, and by maintaining a dialogue between social actors in Peru and in the First World.  It works from an ethical basis inspired by the preferential option for the poor.

The Centre for Studies and Publications (CEP) was set up in 1970 and played a key role in setting up the IBC, with which it has maintained the closet of relationship over the years. Much of the work in the field of education, reflection and publications is carried out jointly with the IBC and the specific role of CEP is to prepare and publish materials which support the training and outreach work of the IBC.  CEP aims to develop educational materials and events to support community leaders and youth leaders commited to social justice and personal and social development.</narrative>
  </description>
